  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 923 PM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nUpper level ridging (near the 95th percentile for this time of year) \nand mild southerly flow will remain in place through Saturday with \nwarm and dry conditions persisting. Increasing southerly flow on \nSaturday may again yield limited fire weather concerns for a few \nareas. \n\nA cold front will move across the area later Saturday or Sunday \nmorning (recent models are a bit slower) bringing a chance for \nshowers and maybe a thunderstorm. Models continue to look rather \nanemic with rainfall totals, with current guidance suggesting a \nquarter inch or less for most areas. Temperatures do look to cool \nsignificantly behind the front, back towards seasonal normals, with \nhighs in the lower 50s and lows near freezing early next week. There \nis another weak signal for a storm system around next Tuesday or \nWednesday.",
